{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_how_it_works_methodology", "label": "How It Works \u2014 Methodology & Honesty", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_baseline", "label": "Load-Everything-Every-Time Baseline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "The one honesty caveat", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All savings are measured against re-reading the entire corpus from scratch on every turn \u2014 a world nobody actually works in. The baseline is deliberately generous, so every figure is framed as directional ('a sense of scale'), not an invoice."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_efficiency_cap", "label": "99.9% Efficiency Cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "The one honesty caveat", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Even if the math rounds to a perfect 100% saving, the dashboard never claims it: recall is cheap but never free, so a fake 100% would be a lie. The hard cap makes that explicit."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_illustrative_projection", "label": "Illustrative Monthly Projection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "Every assumption, stated plainly", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Graphify keeps no per-query log, so it cannot know how many graph queries were actually run. Any 'saved this month' number assumes graphifyAssumedQueriesPerDay (default 8) and is labelled 'illustrative' on its face rather than presented as a measurement."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_mem_formula", "label": "claude-mem Savings Formula", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "The formulas, exactly", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "saved = workTokens \u2212 observations \u00d7 recallTokensPerObservation: producing knowledge the first time is expensive, recalling it is cheap, and the gap is the saving. Efficiency = saving as % of work, capped at 99.9%."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_gfx_formula", "label": "Graphify Savings Formula", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "The formulas, exactly", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "savedTokensPerQuery = corpusTokensNaive \u2212 avgQueryTokens; the one-time build cost from cost.json is always shown alongside, so per-query wins are presented honestly against the real investment that unlocked them."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_discovery_tokens", "label": "discovery_tokens Column", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "claude-mem: where the numbers come from", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For each observation, the tokens it cost to originally produce that piece of knowledge \u2014 the reading, reasoning, and exploration that surfaced it the first time. Summed, it becomes the headline 'work captured'."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_benchmark", "label": "graphify benchmark Command", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "Graphify: where the numbers come from", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_cost_json", "label": "cost.json Build Ledger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "Graphify: where the numbers come from", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Building the graph isn't free \u2014 it costs tokens once. Reading cost.json lets the dashboard show graph savings honestly against their one-time build cost."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_failsafe", "label": "Fail-Safe Collector Behavior", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "Data flow", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any unexpected error writes a partial file with an errors[] array and still exits 0, so a SessionStart hook never blocks a Claude session; worst case the dashboard keeps the previous successful run's data."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_privacy", "label": "Local-Only Privacy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "Privacy: nothing leaves your machine", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The collector reads local files read-only (sqlite3 -readonly), runs local CLIs, and writes local files; the dashboard is a static page opened from disk. No network call, no telemetry, no upload \u2014 observations, code, queries, and token counts never leave the machine."}, {"id": "docs_how_it_works_graphify_history", "label": "graphify-history.json Accruing State", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "What's committed vs regenerated", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only intentionally committed data file: Graphify has no per-query log, so its daily reduction history can only be preserved by appending one snapshot per day and committing it \u2014 everything else under data/ is a disposable, machine-specific cache."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_how_it_works_methodology", "target": "docs_install_guide", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_collector", "target": "docs_how_it_works_benchmark", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_collector", "target": "docs_how_it_works_cost_json", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_failsafe", "target": "readme_sessionstart_hook", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": "Data flow", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_baseline", "target": "docs_how_it_works_mem_formula", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_baseline", "target": "docs_how_it_works_gfx_formula", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_efficiency_cap", "target": "docs_how_it_works_mem_formula", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_illustrative_projection", "target": "docs_how_it_works_gfx_formula", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_mem_formula", "target": "docs_how_it_works_discovery_tokens", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_how_it_works_discovery_tokens", "target": "readme_claude_mem", "relation": "conceptually_related_to"